   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">function</span> allocate <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_06503\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_06503]</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">[[nodiscard]] void * allocate (<a class=\"cppref\" href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t\" title=\"cppreference.com (C++17)\">std::size_t</a> bytes, <a class=\"cppref\" href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t\" title=\"cppreference.com (C++17)\">std::size_t</a> alignment=alignof(<a class=\"cppref\" href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/max_align_t\" title=\"cppreference.com (C++17)\">std::max_align_t</a>)) noexcept;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>As per corresponding usage in [mem.res] except for the following deviations: 1. The function is noexcept 2. The function returns nullptr instead of (potentially) throwing a std::bad_alloc exception</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
